    <div class="home-hero-badge">⚡ LoadRunner Performance Engineering Toolkit</div>
    <h1>LRE Script Generation Toolkit</h1>
    <p class="home-hero-sub">Three tools that generate production-ready LoadRunner VuGen scripts without writing code manually. Pick the tool that matches your starting point below.</p>
    <div class="hero-badges">
      <span class="chip">📂 Postman · Bruno · JMeter</span>
      <span class="chip">🟦 DevWeb JS</span>
      <span class="chip">🟧 VuGen C</span>
      <span class="chip">🔒 In-memory only</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Tool Cards -->
  <div class="tool-cards">

    <!-- Converter card -->
    <div class="tool-card tc-blue" role="button" tabindex="0"
         onclick="switchPortalTab('converter')"
         onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter'||event.key===' ')switchPortalTab('converter')">
      <div class="tc-icon tc-icon-blue">📂</div>
      <span class="tc-tag tc-tag-blue">Collections &amp; JMX → VuGen</span>
      <div class="tc-title">Converter</div>
      <div class="tc-desc">Convert your existing Postman/Bruno API collections or JMeter scripts into VuGen scripts. No scripting knowledge needed — upload your file, choose your output format, and download.</div>
      <ul class="tc-features">
        <li>Postman v2.1 JSON · Bruno JSON, YAML, .bru · JMeter .jmx</li>
        <li>Output: DevWeb (JavaScript) or Web HTTP/HTML (C)</li>
        <li>Authentication: OAuth2, Basic, Bearer, API Key, JWT, AWS Sig v4</li>
        <li>Multi-script mode — one script per folder or thread group</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="tc-cta">
        <span class="tc-cta-text">Open Converter</span>
        <span class="tc-cta-arrow">→</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Recorder card -->
    <div class="tool-card tc-green" role="button" tabindex="0"
         onclick="switchPortalTab('recorder')"
         onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter'||event.key===' ')switchPortalTab('recorder')">
      <div class="tc-icon tc-icon-green">🎙</div>
      <span class="tc-tag tc-tag-green">HAR File → VuGen Script</span>
      <div class="tc-title">Recorder</div>
      <div class="tc-desc">VuGen recording is unavailable on VCSE machines. This tool bypasses that entirely. Install the bookmarklet, record your browser journey, export a HAR from DevTools, and get a ready-to-open VuGen script — no VuGen needed for recording.</div>
      <ul class="tc-features">
        <li>No VuGen installation required to record</li>
        <li>Works with Chrome and Firefox DevTools exports</li>
        <li>Filter domains and mark transaction boundaries visually</li>
        <li>Output: DevWeb (JavaScript) or Web HTTP/HTML (C)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="tc-cta">
        <span class="tc-cta-text">Open Recorder</span>
        <span class="tc-cta-arrow">→</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Script Studio card -->
    <div class="tool-card tc-purple" role="button" tabindex="0"
         onclick="switchPortalTab('studio')"
         onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter'||event.key===' ')switchPortalTab('studio')">
      <div class="tc-icon tc-icon-purple">🧪</div>
      <span class="tc-tag tc-tag-purple">HAR Correlation Engine</span>
      <div class="tc-title">Script Studio</div>
      <div class="tc-desc">Upload one or two HAR files to generate a correlated script. With two HAR files (same journey recorded twice), it compares both recordings and identifies every dynamic value — producing far more complete correlation than a single recording can.</div>
      <ul class="tc-features">
        <li>1 HAR — pattern-based correlation (faster, fewer correlations)</li>
        <li>2 HARs — diff analysis (deeper, more complete correlation)</li>
        <li>Auto-extracts JSON paths, XPath, boundaries, cookies, headers</li>
        <li>Output: DevWeb (JavaScript) or Web HTTP/HTML (C)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="tc-cta">
        <span class="tc-cta-text">Open Script Studio</span>
        <span class="tc-cta-arrow">→</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Which tool do I need? -->
